.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt ACAGE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm acage
.Nd run coding agents in disposable Alpine Linux virtual machines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm install | create
.Op Ar name
.Op Fl nvy
.Op Fl -allow-lan
.Op Fl -backend Ar backend
.Op Fl -disk Ar GB
.Op Fl -harness Ar list
.Op Fl -no-doas
.Op Fl -no-wait
.Op Fl -password
.Op Fl -pool-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -ram Ar MB
.Op Fl -share Ar dir
.Op Fl -ssh-pubkey Ar file
.Op Fl -user Ar user
.Op Fl -vcpus Ar N
.Nm
.Cm image
.Op Fl ny
.Nm
.Cm attach
.Ar name
.Op Fl -agent | Fl -user
.Nm
.Cm push
.Ar name
.Ar path ...
.Op Fl -agent | Fl -user
.Op Fl -to Ar dir
.Nm
.Cm ssh
.Ar name
.Op Fl -agent | Fl -user
.Op Fl - Ar command ...
.Nm
.Cm start | stop | console | delete
.Ar name
.Op Fl ny
.Nm
.Cm list
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
downloads Alpine Linux's official cloud image, verifies its checksum and
signature, and boots a virtual machine from it in which a coding agent can
run with its own kernel, away from the host.
On first boot the machine creates two accounts that both accept the given
SSH key:
.Ql agent ,
which runs the AI and has no root, and one for the invoking user, which gets
root through
.Xr doas 1 .
The agent cannot run anything as the other account and neither can read the
other's home directory.
The machine also installs
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr vim 1 ,
Node.js and the chosen agent harnesses, and starts a firewall that lets it
reach the internet but not the local network or the host.
Nothing from the host is shared with the machine unless
.Fl -share
is given.
.Pp
The commands are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install Op Ar name
Run
.Cm image ,
then
.Cm create .
.It Cm image
Make sure the newest Alpine UEFI cloud image is in the cache
.Pq Pa ~/.cache/agentcage/images ,
downloading it only when a newer release than the cached one is published.
A download is checked against the SHA-512 checksum Alpine publishes and the
GPG signature on it, verified in a temporary keyring against the key shipped
with
.Nm .
After a newer image is verified the previous one is removed, and if Alpine
cannot be reached the newest cached image is used.
The fingerprint is shown for comparison with the one published at
.Lk https://alpinelinux.org/cloud/
unless
.Fl y
is given.
If any check fails, the download is discarded.
.It Cm create Op Ar name
Create and boot a machine from the downloaded image.
Unless
.Fl -no-wait
is given,
.Nm
then waits for first boot to finish, checks that the agents run, adds an
entry to
.Pa ~/.ssh/config ,
and, when run from a terminal, offers to store API keys in the machine,
to generate a GitHub deploy key in it, and to connect.
.It Cm attach Ar name
Log in to the machine at its current address, asking whether as
.Ql agent
or as the invoking user's account, unless
.Fl -agent
or
.Fl -user
is given.
.It Cm push Ar name Ar path ...
Copy files and directories from the host into the home directory of
.Ql agent ,
or of the invoking user's account with
.Fl -user ,
or into
.Ar dir
inside it with
.Fl -to .
The host starts the copy and data only flows into the machine, over SSH.
Symbolic links are copied as links, not followed.
The home directory and credential directories such as
.Pa ~/.ssh
are refused, and files that look like secrets are warned about.
There is no command to copy files out of a machine.
.It Cm ssh Ar name Op Fl - Ar command ...
Log in as
.Ql agent ,
or as the invoking user's account with
.Fl -user ,
and run
.Ar command
if given.
.It Cm start Ar name
Start a stopped machine.
.It Cm stop Ar name
Shut a machine down cleanly, forcing it off if it does not stop within a
minute.
.It Cm console Ar name
Attach to the serial console
.Pq libvirt
or follow the boot output
.Pq qemu .
.It Cm list
List the machines
.Nm
created.
.It Cm delete Ar name
List what will be removed and, after confirmation, delete the machine, its
disk, its SSH configuration entry and host key, and the settings saved for
it.
A shared directory that
.Nm
created is offered for deletion separately, defaulting to no; one that
existed before is kept, and
.Fl y
never deletes it.
Leftovers of a machine whose creation failed are cleaned up too.
Machines
.Nm
did not create are refused.
.El
.Pp
Settings for
.Cm install
and
.Cm create
that are not given as options are asked for when running in a terminal;
otherwise the defaults below are used.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -agent , Fl -user
With
.Cm attach ,
.Cm push
and
.Cm ssh :
log in as
.Ql agent
or as the invoking user's account.
.It Fl -allow-lan
Leave the firewall out, so the machine can reach the local network and the
host.
.It Fl -to Ar dir
With
.Cm push :
copy into
.Ar dir ,
relative to the home directory, instead of the home directory itself.
.It Fl -backend Ar backend
.Cm libvirt
.Pq the default
defines the machine on the
.Li qemu:///system
connection.
.Cm qemu
runs
.Xr qemu-system-x86_64 1
directly as the invoking user, without libvirt.
.It Fl -disk Ar GB
Disk size.
The disk starts small and can grow to this size.
The default is 10.
.It Fl -harness Ar list
Comma-separated agent harnesses to install:
.Cm pi ,
.Cm claude-code ,
.Cm codex ,
or
.Cm none .
The default is
.Cm pi .
.It Fl -name Ar name
Name of the machine, also its hostname and SSH alias.
It can also be given as the argument after the command.
The default is
.Li agentcage .
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Print what would be changed instead of changing it.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Print each command as it runs, and show cloud-init's progress and the tail of
its log while waiting for first boot, instead of waiting silently.
.It Fl -no-doas
Do not give the invoking user's account root either, so nobody in the
machine can become root.
.It Fl -password
Ask for a password for the invoking user's account.
Only its SHA-512 crypt hash is put in the machine.
.Xr doas 1
then asks for it, and it works for console login and
.Xr su 1 .
Without it the account has no password and
.Xr doas 1
does not ask for one.
SSH login is key-only either way.
.It Fl -pool-dir Ar dir
Where images and disks are kept.
The choice is saved and used by later commands.
With libvirt the default is
.Pa /var/lib/libvirt/images/agentcage ,
or
.Pa /home/agentcage
when
.Pa /
is a separate filesystem with less free space than
.Pa /home .
With qemu it is
.Pa ~/.local/share/agentcage .
.It Fl -ram Ar MB
Memory, at least 512.
The default is 2048.
.It Fl -share Ar dir
Make
.Ar dir
appear read-write as
.Pa ~/shared
in the
.Ql agent
account, which gets the invoking user's uid.
.Nm
prints what this exposes and asks for
.Ql share
to be typed before going on.
It refuses
.Pa / ,
the home directory, anything containing it, and credential directories
such as
.Pa ~/.ssh .
A missing
.Ar dir
is created after the confirmation.
.It Fl -ssh-pubkey Ar file
Public key to authorize for the guest user.
The default is
.Pa ~/.ssh/id_agentcage.pub ,
generated if missing.
.It Fl -user Ar user
With
.Cm install
and
.Cm create :
name of the invoking user's account in the machine; anything but
.Ql agent .
The default is the invoking user's name.
.It Fl -vcpus Ar N
Number of virtual CPUs.
The default is 2.
.It Fl -no-wait
Start the machine and return without waiting for first boot.
.It Fl y , Fl -yes
Do not ask for confirmation: of the image key fingerprint, of the
shared-folder warning, or before deleting.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a summary of commands and options.
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Pp
Before creating anything,
.Nm
checks that every required host tool is installed, reporting all that are
missing at once with a command to install them, and that the pool directory's
filesystem has room for the full disk size, plus 5 GB that stays free when it
is the root filesystem.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev AGENTCAGE_BACKEND
Backend to use when
.Fl -backend
is not given.
.It Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME , XDG_CONFIG_HOME , XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directories for the download cache, the settings file and the qemu
pool, as in the XDG Base Directory specification.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/agentcage/config
Saved settings, such as the pool directory.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/id_agentcage
Default SSH key.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
Each machine gets an entry between
.Ql # agentcage:begin Ar name
and
.Ql # agentcage:end Ar name .
.Cm attach ,
.Cm ssh
and
.Cm push
rewrite its address when the machine's has changed, so plain
.Ql ssh Ar name
keeps working after a new DHCP lease.
.It Pa /var/lib/libvirt/images/agentcage
Default libvirt pool.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/agentcage
Default qemu pool.
.It Pa /mnt/acage-shared/ Ns Ar name
Suggested shared directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Cm create
also fails when the machine never becomes reachable over SSH.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a machine with Claude Code and connect to it:
.Pp
.Dl $ acage install mybox --harness claude-code
.Dl $ acage attach mybox
.Pp
Give the agent a project to work on:
.Pp
.Dl $ acage push mybox ~/projects/app
.Pp
Install a package as yourself, since the agent has no root:
.Pp
.Dl $ acage ssh mybox --user -- doas apk add neovim
.Pp
Run a command as the agent and copy the output to the host clipboard:
.Pp
.Dl $ acage ssh mybox -- cat '~/notes.md' | wl-copy
.Pp
See what a machine would look like without changing anything:
.Pp
.Dl $ acage create test --harness codex --no-doas -n
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qemu-system-x86_64 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr virsh 1 ,
.Xr doas.conf 5 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The machine can reach the internet, so an agent can send anything it can
read inside the machine there.
The firewall that keeps it off the local network and the host runs inside the
machine: the agent cannot change it, but anything that gains root in the
machine can.
With
.Fl -allow-lan
there is no firewall, and with
.Fl -backend Cm qemu
the host's loopback interface is then reachable through 10.0.2.2.
.Pp
A shared directory is fully readable and writable by the agent, and files
written there are on the host.
With libvirt it is served by a process running as root, so root in the
machine, which the agent does not have, can create root-owned and setuid
files in it.
.Pp
Agent packages are installed from npm at their latest versions on first
boot.
.Pp
.Nm
refuses to run as root, which would place the SSH key, settings and the
machine login in root's home and undo the isolation; the libvirt backend
elevates with
.Xr sudo 8
only where it must.
.Pp
See
.Pa SECURITY.md
in the source distribution for the full threat model.
